\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k(T-{T}_{S}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${T}_{S}$ is the temperature of the surroundings, and $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.\n\nIn our case, ${T}_{S}={35}^{∘}\\text{C},$ and we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k(T-35).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672727 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "790823da-d3ca-5323-814f-de9286dc80bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{T}^{′}(t)=kT(T-70)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672711} {:answer/id #uuid "b7e9d369-2677-5dfa-9910-3e1a09c8374c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{T}^{′}(t)=-k(T+70)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672720} {:answer/id #uuid "ba0ad2af-a525-5d42-ab36-45c260029c2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{T}^{′}(t)=-kT(T-70)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672721} {:answer/id #uuid "cef92983-1935-54c2-bc91-99f0b03c7949" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{T}^{′}(t)=-k(T-70)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672724} {:answer/id #uuid "d4e1736e-a36a-5ccf-abb4-37d5783bd6f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{T}^{′}(t)=k(T-70)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672725}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672724} :answer-field/id #uuid "e15f2f6b-753f-59e6-83f9-114506d09104" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672726}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e423b9ad-3262-58aa-a896-09efb5972d47" :question/problem "The rate at which a freshly baked cake cools is proportional to the difference between its temperature and the temperature of its surroundings. Let $T(t)$ be the temperature of the cake in degrees Fahrenheit, and let $t>0$ be the time in minutes. If the temperature of the surroundings is ${70}^{∘}\\text{F},$ which differential equation could be used to model the temperature of the cake? Assume that $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality. Write the equation in terms of the given constant $k$." :question/worked-solution "Newton's law of cooling states that the rate at which the temperature $T(t)$ of a body changes is proportional to the difference between its temperature and its surroundings. Therefore, we have the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k(T-{T}_{S}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${T}_{S}$ is the temperature of the surroundings, and $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.\n\nIn our case, ${T}_{S}={70}^{∘}\\text{F},$ and we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k(T-70).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672734 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0be068eb-64c8-59a3-afa7-5664f17d1b0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{115}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672735} {:answer/id #uuid "14ca0aad-76fb-51da-8fca-64986833086a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{109}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672738} {:answer/id #uuid "6163c0dc-e2e5-5bc5-822c-c053738923b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{116}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672747} {:answer/id #uuid "708c015e-8ffa-5dd3-8bdf-3b6335424caf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{111}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672751} {:answer/id #uuid "96a3750a-e8ce-5fd8-a114-550474ae2c1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{113}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672757}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672738} :answer-field/id #uuid "0cd6a476-2f32-513b-b9d7-56d18d395036" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672736}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0bcfe524-d1bc-5602-9bbb-6250eda84ba0" :question/problem "The temperature $T(t),$ in degrees Celsius, of a cooling iron can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dT}{dt}=-0.03(T-30)\n$$\n\nwhere $t>0$ is the time, measured in minutes. If the initial temperature of the iron is ${119}^{∘}C,$ calculate its temperature after $4$ minutes. Round your answer to the nearest integer." :question/worked-solution "We're told that the temperature of the cooling iron is modeled by the inhibited decay equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dT}{dt}=-0.03(T-30).\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate our differential equation by separating the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dT}{T-30} & =-0.03\\,dt \\\\ \\int \\frac{dT}{T-30} & =-\\int 0.03\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|T-30| & =-0.03t+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this is the solution to an inhibited decay equation, we have $T-30>0$ for all $t>0.$\nNext, we solve for $T(t),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T-30 & ={e}^{-0.03t+C} \\\\ T-30 & ={e}^{C}{e}^{-0.03t} \\\\ T-30 & =K{e}^{-0.03t} \\\\ T & =30+K{e}^{-0.03t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $K={e}^{C}$ is a constant of integration. \n\nWe're told that the initial temperature of the iron was ${119}^{∘}C.$ So, we apply the initial condition $T(0)=119,$ and solve for $K:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}119 & =30+K{e}^{0} \\\\ 119 & =30+K \\\\ K & =89\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to our initial value problem is\n\n$$\nT(t)=30+89{e}^{-0.03t}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the temperature of the iron after $t=4$ minutes is\n\n$$\nT(4)=30+89{e}^{-0.03\\cdot 4}≈{109}^{∘}\\text{C},\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672739 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c113558-955c-5204-a915-d21433372a41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{44}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672740} {:answer/id #uuid "34e055a3-ef9f-5de7-b337-ea388b3368b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{39}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672741} {:answer/id #uuid "59d7abd4-e8b4-5fb6-9c0e-a26d63d65981" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{40}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672745} {:answer/id #uuid "69df54c2-ee15-5a9b-a0b9-ba288365db68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{43}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672748} {:answer/id #uuid "81e12548-0078-542b-a7be-ebccf5ee0831" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{42}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672755}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672740} :answer-field/id #uuid "d517d6ae-4a01-559e-a78d-ff71eb2425d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672762}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "20cf5dff-13d7-53c1-80a8-f2d47d353696" :question/problem "The temperature $T(t),$ in degrees Celsius, of a body can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dT}{dt}=-0.08(T-33)\n$$\n\nwhere $t>0$ is the time, measured in minutes. If the initial temperature of the body is ${55}^{∘}C,$ calculate the temperature of the body after $9$ minutes. Round your answer to the nearest integer." :question/worked-solution "We're told that the temperature of the body is modeled by the inhibited decay equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dT}{dt}=-0.08(T-33).\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate our differential equation by separating the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dT}{T-33} & =-0.08\\,dt \\\\ \\int \\frac{dT}{T-33} & =-\\int 0.08\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|T-33| & =-0.08t+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this is the solution to an inhibited decay equation, we have $T-33>0$ for all $t>0.$\nNext, we solve for $T(t),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T-33 & ={e}^{-0.08t+C} \\\\ T-33 & ={e}^{C}{e}^{-0.08t} \\\\ T-33 & =K{e}^{-0.08t} \\\\ T & =33+K{e}^{-0.08t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $K={e}^{C}$ is a constant of integration. \n\nWe're told that the initial temperature of the body was ${55}^{∘}C.$ So, we apply the initial condition $T(0)=55,$ and solve for $K:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}55 & =33+K{e}^{0} \\\\ 55 & =33+K \\\\ K & =22\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to our initial value problem is\n\n$$\nT(t)=33+22{e}^{-0.08t}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the temperature of the body after $t=9$ minutes is\n\n$$\nT(9)=33+22{e}^{-0.08\\cdot 9}≈{44}^{∘}\\text{C},\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672746 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0496ce21-94ad-5059-9245-6e93db58d821" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{58}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672732} {:answer/id #uuid "3f3555e7-76cc-58b7-b084-57a457f82ac7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{55}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672742} {:answer/id #uuid "d337d87b-784c-5884-85d9-dde8eef8b832" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{61}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672761} {:answer/id #uuid "e2e45505-5515-5a20-97a9-f1eaa6ec8d40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{53}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672764} {:answer/id #uuid "e54193fa-674b-57bd-b84b-d76431906b6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{59}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672765}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672742} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b78b1b8-fbe7-50fe-a450-31525c7b8ea4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672759}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5a5a1d59-ffa3-514b-bca9-b5126ed8e4bf" :question/problem "The temperature $T(t),$ in degrees Celsius, of a compressor of a refrigerator can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dT}{dt}=-0.09(T-34)\n$$\n\nwhere $t>0$ is the time, measured in minutes. If the initial temperature of the compressor is ${96}^{∘}C,$ calculate the temperature of the compressor after $12$ minutes. Round your answer to the nearest integer." :question/worked-solution "We're told that the temperature of the compressor of a refrigerator is modeled by the inhibited decay equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dT}{dt}=-0.09(T-34).\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate our differential equation by separating the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dT}{T-34} & =-0.09\\,dt \\\\ \\int \\frac{dT}{T-34} & =-\\int 0.09\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|T-34| & =-0.09t+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this is the solution to an inhibited decay equation, we have $T-34>0$ for all $t>0.$\nNext, we solve for $T(t),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T-34 & ={e}^{-0.09t+C} \\\\ T-34 & ={e}^{C}{e}^{-0.09t} \\\\ T-34 & =K{e}^{-0.09t} \\\\ T & =34+K{e}^{-0.09t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $K={e}^{C}$ is a constant of integration. \n\nWe're told that the initial temperature of the compressor was ${96}^{∘}C.$ So, we apply the initial condition $T(0)=96,$ and solve for $K:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}96 & =34+K{e}^{0} \\\\ 96 & =34+K \\\\ K & =62\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to our initial value problem is\n\n$$\nT(t)=34+62{e}^{-0.09t}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the temperature of the compressor after $t=12$ minutes is\n\n$$\nT(12)=34+62{e}^{-0.09\\cdot 12}≈{55}^{∘}\\text{C},\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672752 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08567872-9496-590d-8e6f-b30e71703fed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{86}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672733} {:answer/id #uuid "43c21da3-ea72-5125-be19-3be6a575a8f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{85}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672743} {:answer/id #uuid "6acbf7bf-3831-5363-bd01-e7054b0eadf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{79}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672749} {:answer/id #uuid "78871fa2-3d48-5d31-a760-6b331565db36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{84}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672753} {:answer/id #uuid "9363bab4-0b88-5da7-9187-b6087fb174fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{80}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672756}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672753} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2f37b8e-125b-5fb2-bef1-4f975e2143e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672760}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7220076f-7a8f-59d7-a472-6fa27abeba93" :question/problem "The temperature $T(t),$ in degrees Celsius, of a cooling iron can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dT}{dt}=-0.15(T-34)\n$$\n\nwhere $t>0$ is the time, measured in minutes. If the initial temperature of the iron is ${176}^{∘}C,$ calculate its temperature after $7$ minutes. Round your answer to the nearest integer." :question/worked-solution "We're told that the temperature of the cooling iron is modeled by the inhibited decay equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dT}{dt}=-0.15(T-34).\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate our differential equation by separating the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dT}{T-34} & =-0.15\\,dt \\\\ \\int \\frac{dT}{T-34} & =-\\int 0.15\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|T-34| & =-0.15t+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this is the solution to an inhibited decay equation, we have $T-34>0$ for all $t>0.$\nNext, we solve for $T(t),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T-34 & ={e}^{-0.15t+C} \\\\ T-34 & ={e}^{C}{e}^{-0.15t} \\\\ T-34 & =K{e}^{-0.15t} \\\\ T & =34+K{e}^{-0.15t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $K={e}^{C}$ is a constant of integration. \n\nWe're told that the initial temperature of the iron was ${176}^{∘}C.$ So, we apply the initial condition $T(0)=176,$ and solve for $K:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}176 & =34+K{e}^{0} \\\\ 176 & =34+K \\\\ K & =142\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to our initial value problem is\n\n$$\nT(t)=34+142{e}^{-0.15t}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the temperature of the iron after $t=7$ minutes is\n\n$$\nT(7)=34+142{e}^{-0.15\\cdot 7}≈{84}^{∘}\\text{C},\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672758 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13855e76-e295-5d9a-8d11-1c293c24822e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{57}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672737} {:answer/id #uuid "535f5b1f-e65c-5148-9576-c6d54a0f7ee7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{56}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672744} {:answer/id #uuid "6f49ad19-3571-500e-bae9-8b2b72dc7975" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{53}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672750} {:answer/id #uuid "7a2ff935-e641-5936-a4ec-1a5e21cee286" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{58}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672754} {:answer/id #uuid "f6ddc331-dc9a-5453-bcbd-7038f002203f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{52}^{∘}\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672766}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186672750} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6b2f37f-52a6-5af2-a3b8-26d28c39951d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186672763}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "980a5957-ed65-5e73-85e5-566f07d47b61" :question/problem "The temperature $T(t),$ in degrees Celsius, of a fluorescent light bulb after turning off can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dT}{dt}=-0.07(T-34)\n$$\n\nwhere $t>0$ is the time, measured in minutes. If the initial temperature of the bulb is ${65}^{∘}C,$ calculate the temperature of the bulb after $7$ minutes. Round your answer to the nearest integer." :question/worked-solution "We're told that the temperature of the fluorescent light bulb is modeled by the inhibited decay equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dT}{dt}=-0.07(T-34).\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate our differential equation by separating the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dT}{T-34} & =-0.07\\,dt \\\\ \\int \\frac{dT}{T-34} & =-\\int 0.07\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|T-34| & =-0.07t+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this is the solution to an inhibited decay equation, we have $T-34>0$ for all $t>0.$\nNext, we solve for $T(t),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T-34 & ={e}^{-0.07t+C} \\\\ T-34 & ={e}^{C}{e}^{-0.07t} \\\\ T-34 & =K{e}^{-0.07t} \\\\ T & =34+K{e}^{-0.07t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $K={e}^{C}$ is a constant of integration. \n\nWe're told that the initial temperature of the bulb was ${65}^{∘}C.$ So, we apply the initial condition $T(0)=65,$ and solve for $K:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}65 & =34+K{e}^{0} \\\\ 65 & =34+K \\\\ K & =31\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to our initial value problem is\n\n$$\nT(t)=34+31{e}^{-0.07t}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the temperature of the bulb after $t=7$ minutes is\n\n$$\nT(7)=34+31{e}^{-0.07\\cdot 7}≈{53}^{∘}\\text{C},\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673462 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31b7ed29-4110-5439-9fea-1fe2b4583f85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(- \\frac{1}{v + 4 \\sin{\\left(v \\right)}}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673457} {:answer/id #uuid "4c9c6a35-d392-522a-80cc-5014ad8056d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(- \\frac{1}{2 v + 4 \\sin{\\left(v \\right)}}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673464} {:answer/id #uuid "6644b445-588b-5876-ac12-16fcbbbdb6a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(- \\frac{1}{4 \\sin{\\left(v \\right)}}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673467} {:answer/id #uuid "9c104760-c4ea-5254-8ee6-9607c45f3fd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(\\frac{1}{2 v - 4 \\sin{\\left(v \\right)}}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673476} {:answer/id #uuid "ff0e5061-c0c2-5c3c-a819-8e1d3da4a959" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(\\frac{1}{v - 4 \\sin{\\left(v \\right)}}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673488}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673476} :answer-field/id #uuid "8efda5f6-daac-5eaa-9c33-8ade9b1df601" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673474}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "44130cf3-5c16-5af7-b9f5-b2de7d578046" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=- 4 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{y}{x} \\right)} + \\frac{3 y}{x}.\n$$\n\nIf the transformation $y=v(x)x$ is applied to the differential equation, what is the resulting equation?" :question/worked-solution "Using the transformation $y=vx$ (where $v=v(x)$), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given differential equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =- 4 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{y}{x} \\right)} + \\frac{3 y}{x} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =3 v - 4 \\sin{\\left(v \\right)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =3 v - 4 \\sin{\\left(v \\right)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =2 v - 4 \\sin{\\left(v \\right)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =2 v - 4 \\sin{\\left(v \\right)} \\\\ \\left(\\frac{1}{2 v - 4 \\sin{\\left(v \\right)}}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673463 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61513150-7cee-53e3-a880-9c941cc085cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(\\frac{v^{2} + 1}{v^{2} - v + 3}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673466} {:answer/id #uuid "8c2d19bf-82f4-529a-bb11-0355361a26e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(\\frac{v^{2} + 1}{v^{3} + v^{2} + 3}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673470} {:answer/id #uuid "8e1dc5ba-fca7-57d0-bf9f-ccc6a737a032" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(\\frac{- v^{2} - 1}{3 v^{3} - v^{2} + 4 v - 3}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673471} {:answer/id #uuid "9ea65024-06bf-5c9e-90f7-b27f6baf4a3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(\\frac{- v^{2} - 1}{v^{3} - v^{2} + 2 v - 3}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673477} {:answer/id #uuid "caf06db2-5371-5393-9a4a-7a1c5fcd5938" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(\\frac{- v^{2} - 1}{2 v^{3} - v^{2} + 3 v - 3}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673483}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673477} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd2d9f09-fd5b-5b85-ae01-0b084a69cbaf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673486}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "467974b8-3dec-53ec-b6d7-428e15add07c" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3 x^{2} - x y + y^{2}}{x^{2} + y^{2}}.\n$$\n\nIf the transformation $y=v(x)x$ is applied to the differential equation, what is the resulting equation?" :question/worked-solution "Using the transformation $y=vx$ (where $v=v(x)$), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given differential equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{3 x^{2} - x y + y^{2}}{x^{2} + y^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{v^{2} x^{2} - v x^{2} + 3 x^{2}}{v^{2} x^{2} + x^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{v^{2} - v + 3}{v^{2} + 1} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =- v + \\frac{v^{2} - v + 3}{v^{2} + 1} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{- v^{3} + v^{2} - 2 v + 3}{v^{2} + 1} \\\\ \\left(\\frac{- v^{2} - 1}{v^{3} - v^{2} + 2 v - 3}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673469 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9835353f-47a9-50dd-bea7-c7e5c1fd97bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(\\frac{1}{v + e^{\\sin{\\left(4 v \\right)}}}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673475} {:answer/id #uuid "ad34913f-f4d8-5ec1-803c-4a152c51395b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(- \\frac{1}{v - e^{\\sin{\\left(4 v \\right)}}}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673479} {:answer/id #uuid "b9b73026-e5d3-5ecd-a3fc-9e97e058f89d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(e^{- \\sin{\\left(4 v \\right)}}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673481} {:answer/id #uuid "d187a694-b484-5f75-b414-beb952203ef1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(- \\frac{1}{3 v - e^{\\sin{\\left(4 v \\right)}}}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673485} {:answer/id #uuid "f7d6d6dc-76da-566d-a8ea-649b26e0f1d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(- \\frac{1}{2 v - e^{\\sin{\\left(4 v \\right)}}}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673487}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673485} :answer-field/id #uuid "b80ca885-09c2-5723-879f-aa276818f477" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673480}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7ccdf364-5a39-524d-81ba-a51238dcb753" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=e^{\\sin{\\left(\\frac{4 y}{x} \\right)}} - \\frac{2 y}{x}.\n$$\n\nIf the transformation $y=v(x)x$ is applied to the differential equation, what is the resulting equation?" :question/worked-solution "Using the transformation $y=vx$ (where $v=v(x)$), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given differential equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =e^{\\sin{\\left(\\frac{4 y}{x} \\right)}} - \\frac{2 y}{x} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =- 2 v + e^{\\sin{\\left(4 v \\right)}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =- 2 v + e^{\\sin{\\left(4 v \\right)}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =- 3 v + e^{\\sin{\\left(4 v \\right)}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =- 3 v + e^{\\sin{\\left(4 v \\right)}} \\\\ \\left(- \\frac{1}{3 v - e^{\\sin{\\left(4 v \\right)}}}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673472 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0971104e-1df2-59ea-b87d-7cd78122cf76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(\\frac{1}{v + e^{\\sin{\\left(4 v \\right)}}}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673454} {:answer/id #uuid "3e5f0442-4438-535f-886a-9d1680990fc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(- \\frac{1}{3 v - e^{\\sin{\\left(4 v \\right)}}}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673459} {:answer/id #uuid "3fb4cb01-32b9-5648-a9c2-4708e176d91c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(e^{- \\sin{\\left(4 v \\right)}}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673461} {:answer/id #uuid "4f98df25-e0ca-5a59-84b5-5838c1c63dd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(- \\frac{1}{v - e^{\\sin{\\left(4 v \\right)}}}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673465} {:answer/id #uuid "c7d73034-6248-53cb-af52-c3fe4c077431" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(- \\frac{1}{2 v - e^{\\sin{\\left(4 v \\right)}}}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673482}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673465} :answer-field/id #uuid "aadfed3e-dbfa-5654-9370-1c1763dee7fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673478}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8e41f52e-5fe8-545f-84ca-128c71ca7aaa" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=e^{\\sin{\\left(\\frac{4 y}{x} \\right)}}.\n$$\n\nIf the transformation $y=v(x)x$ is applied to the differential equation, what is the resulting equation?" :question/worked-solution "Using the transformation $y=vx$ (where $v=v(x)$), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given differential equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =e^{\\sin{\\left(\\frac{4 y}{x} \\right)}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =e^{\\sin{\\left(4 v \\right)}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =e^{\\sin{\\left(4 v \\right)}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =- v + e^{\\sin{\\left(4 v \\right)}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =- v + e^{\\sin{\\left(4 v \\right)}} \\\\ \\left(- \\frac{1}{v - e^{\\sin{\\left(4 v \\right)}}}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673473 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15eee99b-6f3d-515b-9d6f-43471d08138c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sec{\\left(\\frac{3}{v} \\right)}}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673455} {:answer/id #uuid "230a53b5-1e03-589b-9bfa-e8aab4db801a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(\\frac{1}{2 v + \\sec{\\left(\\frac{3}{v} \\right)}}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673456} {:answer/id #uuid "34289676-1ab7-572f-bb26-c148fecbd449" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(- \\frac{1}{2 v - \\sec{\\left(\\frac{3}{v} \\right)}}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673458} {:answer/id #uuid "6d330680-f87a-598f-baff-4b5aef3a24f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(- \\frac{1}{v - \\sec{\\left(\\frac{3}{v} \\right)}}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673468} {:answer/id #uuid "cf1c9a96-4346-5200-9709-5f7174852b4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(\\frac{1}{v + \\sec{\\left(\\frac{3}{v} \\right)}}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673484}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673468} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f1f997e-32b1-55b8-b31d-21179ff85584" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673460}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8ef82846-a542-551b-9346-5d048c648778" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\sec{\\left(\\frac{3 x}{y} \\right)}.\n$$\n\nIf the transformation $y=v(x)x$ is applied to the differential equation, what is the resulting equation?" :question/worked-solution "Using the transformation $y=vx$ (where $v=v(x)$), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given differential equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\sec{\\left(\\frac{3 x}{y} \\right)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\sec{\\left(\\frac{3}{v} \\right)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\sec{\\left(\\frac{3}{v} \\right)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =- v + \\sec{\\left(\\frac{3}{v} \\right)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =- v + \\sec{\\left(\\frac{3}{v} \\right)} \\\\ \\left(- \\frac{1}{v - \\sec{\\left(\\frac{3}{v} \\right)}}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673498 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26f12a2c-f5f0-5b38-80c9-b115d206af76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=Cx^2+6x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673497} {:answer/id #uuid "678f298c-c478-5daf-ab27-245bae154add" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=Cx^2+5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673506} {:answer/id #uuid "7257744d-baf9-52bb-a667-330bb49fec45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=Cx^2+3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673508} {:answer/id #uuid "cf1f52c1-9e2f-5703-bbf2-35294a1c9263" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=Cx^2+7x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673517} {:answer/id #uuid "e6c932a9-2118-59f3-8667-5bfbd109a495" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=Cx^2+4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673522}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673506} :answer-field/id #uuid "103a8f1e-4f0f-51ce-a8a6-ea01b09f1097" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673493}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "30cc31fb-987b-53e1-a0e0-f17337bbd938" :question/problem "Use the transformation $y=v(x)x$ to find the general solution of the following homogeneous differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{-5x+2y}{x}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "With $y=v(x)x$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}+v\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(x) \\\\ &=x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}+v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}+v&=\\frac{-5x+2(vx)}{x} \\\\ x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}+v&=-5+2v \\\\ x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=-5+v \\\\ \\frac{1}{-5+v}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=\\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int\\frac{1}{-5+v}\\,\\mathrm{d}v&=\\int\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ \\ln|v-5|&=\\ln|x|+C_1 \\\\ |v-5|&=e^{C_1}|x| \\\\ v-5&=Cx \\\\ v&=Cx+5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the transformation $y=vx$, we get\n\n$$\nv=\\frac{y}{x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our solution, we finally obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{x}&=Cx+5 \\\\ y&=Cx^2+5x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe signed constant $C$ absorbs $e^{C_1}$. Division by $v-5$ excluded $v=+5$; restoring it permits $C=0$, giving $y=+5x$.\n\nThe solution is used on intervals where $x\\ne0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673503 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d51935d-6604-58ea-9402-f93f14a1c15e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-9x\\ln|x|+Cx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673496} {:answer/id #uuid "514c5fa7-4317-5fce-b10d-b459d799ef56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=9x\\ln|x|+Cx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673504} {:answer/id #uuid "baeffd52-c01a-5250-bb6e-0e51261e9b11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-8x\\ln|x|+Cx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673515} {:answer/id #uuid "e1537f74-01c8-5e66-9e68-8eea3359ff5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-7x\\ln|x|+Cx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673520} {:answer/id #uuid "ea5127ff-9fd8-5f23-9d65-d6cda4e06ade" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=8x\\ln|x|+Cx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673523}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673515} :answer-field/id #uuid "c79074eb-ac8b-5c2b-8b93-3c38f1b8a9ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673516}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4b4c00e1-aa47-5602-bd0d-168e84572944" :question/problem "Use the transformation $y=v(x)x$ to find the general solution of the following homogeneous differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{-8x+y}{x}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "With $y=v(x)x$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}+v\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(x) \\\\ &=x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}+v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}+v&=\\frac{-8x+(vx)}{x} \\\\ x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}+v&=-8+v \\\\ x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=-8 \\\\ \\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=\\frac{-8}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int\\mathrm{d}v&=-8\\int\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ v&=-8\\ln|x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the transformation $y=vx$, we get\n\n$$\nv=\\frac{y}{x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our solution, we finally obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{x}&=-8\\ln|x|+C \\\\ y&=-8x\\ln|x|+Cx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n\n\nThe solution is used on intervals where $x\\ne0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673507 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "108d7439-bcd1-5e26-9eb1-5a008b73b1f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=x\\sqrt[3]{-15\\ln|x|+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673494} {:answer/id #uuid "161567f2-2d20-5482-884c-b7b6aeb3f280" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=x\\sqrt[3]{-9\\ln|x|+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673495} {:answer/id #uuid "3138456f-b7f9-5b66-bc73-30e7df6c24f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=x\\sqrt[3]{-12\\ln|x|+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673499} {:answer/id #uuid "37c60102-735e-5f3f-a2f1-f9c0cf04a103" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=x\\sqrt[3]{-6\\ln|x|+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673500} {:answer/id #uuid "e3b1ebf6-4ad9-5386-b26a-47040c79f52d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=x\\sqrt[3]{-3\\ln|x|+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673521}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673495} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba1e2ba0-cc10-5fde-aafd-f3afb52730fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673514}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6b425fb8-4418-5edc-933b-1ae101a41660" :question/problem "Use the transformation $y=v(x)x$ to find the general solution of the following homogeneous differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{-3x^3+y^3}{xy^2}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "With $y=v(x)x$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}+v\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(x) \\\\ &=x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}+v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}+v&=\\frac{-3x^3+(vx)^3}{x(vx)^2} \\\\ x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}+v&=\\frac{-3+v^3}{v^2}=\\frac{-3}{v^2}+v \\\\ x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=\\frac{-3}{v^2} \\\\ v^2\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=\\frac{-3}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int v^2\\,\\mathrm{d}v&=-3\\int\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ \\frac{v^3}{3}&=-3\\ln|x|+C_1 \\\\ v^3&=-9\\ln|x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the transformation $y=vx$, we get\n\n$$\nv=\\frac{y}{x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our solution, we finally obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left(\\frac{y}{x}\\right)^3&=-9\\ln|x|+C \\\\ y^3&=x^3(-9\\ln|x|+C) \\\\ y&=x\\sqrt[3]{-9\\ln|x|+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere $C=3C_1$ and the cube root is real. Restrict the solution to intervals where $y\\ne0$.\n\nThe solution is used on intervals where $x\\ne0$ and $y\\ne0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673512 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0378c6c1-1689-51b3-8e5d-fb43415a1974" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=x\\sqrt[3]{6\\ln|x|+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673490} {:answer/id #uuid "38955d01-ccd4-560b-9139-6c453f5555a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=x\\sqrt[3]{9\\ln|x|+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673501} {:answer/id #uuid "4898faf8-30ee-573e-bf75-852d9288d67c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=x\\sqrt[3]{18\\ln|x|+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673502} {:answer/id #uuid "9981dd32-3989-5e26-909d-46df1a93e73a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=x\\sqrt[3]{12\\ln|x|+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673510} {:answer/id #uuid "d9893475-8584-50b4-b9fe-32d8380fbe44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=x\\sqrt[3]{15\\ln|x|+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673519}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673502} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec11a14d-eb08-534c-9e8f-f43faa60a50b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673524}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ab3a19b0-a384-5471-b89f-af5746a38437" :question/problem "Use the transformation $y=v(x)x$ to find the general solution of the following homogeneous differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{6x^3+y^3}{xy^2}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "With $y=v(x)x$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}+v\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(x) \\\\ &=x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}+v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}+v&=\\frac{6x^3+(vx)^3}{x(vx)^2} \\\\ x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}+v&=\\frac{6+v^3}{v^2}=\\frac{6}{v^2}+v \\\\ x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=\\frac{6}{v^2} \\\\ v^2\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=\\frac{6}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int v^2\\,\\mathrm{d}v&=6\\int\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ \\frac{v^3}{3}&=6\\ln|x|+C_1 \\\\ v^3&=18\\ln|x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the transformation $y=vx$, we get\n\n$$\nv=\\frac{y}{x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our solution, we finally obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left(\\frac{y}{x}\\right)^3&=18\\ln|x|+C \\\\ y^3&=x^3(18\\ln|x|+C) \\\\ y&=x\\sqrt[3]{18\\ln|x|+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere $C=3C_1$ and the cube root is real. Restrict the solution to intervals where $y\\ne0$.\n\nThe solution is used on intervals where $x\\ne0$ and $y\\ne0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673518 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a7aa767-09c1-5f33-beee-56d2dc091085" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=9x\\ln|x|+Cx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673491} {:answer/id #uuid "0af3e1f8-e33c-58bd-8211-dc7a53c2e32e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-9x\\ln|x|+Cx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673492} {:answer/id #uuid "649a7d8b-200a-5233-af08-7df509c94bad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-6x\\ln|x|+Cx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673505} {:answer/id #uuid "9efd76df-fb57-5448-8be0-69dfed592e9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-7x\\ln|x|+Cx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673511} {:answer/id #uuid "aec599be-75e7-5ce7-b9ec-a7bb418c544b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-8x\\ln|x|+Cx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673513}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673491} :answer-field/id #uuid "81a5f1e5-e390-5a6a-aea6-e93552d4299b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673509}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d2255ee7-abce-50d0-aa0c-7b7dbf70082c" :question/problem "Use the transformation $y=v(x)x$ to find the general solution of the following homogeneous differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{9x+y}{x}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "With $y=v(x)x$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}+v\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(x) \\\\ &=x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}+v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}+v&=\\frac{9x+(vx)}{x} \\\\ x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}+v&=9+v \\\\ x\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=9 \\\\ \\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=\\frac{9}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int\\mathrm{d}v&=9\\int\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ v&=9\\ln|x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the transformation $y=vx$, we get\n\n$$\nv=\\frac{y}{x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our solution, we finally obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{x}&=9\\ln|x|+C \\\\ y&=9x\\ln|x|+Cx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n\n\nThe solution is used on intervals where $x\\ne0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674232 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1911a5a7-f3f7-570f-9fa3-c1981c4207d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-25(-1-2x)^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674225} {:answer/id #uuid "2af3b741-0e3b-5d69-b4c9-aeec185861b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6(-1-2x)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674228} {:answer/id #uuid "3ee743cc-f41a-5f09-bc26-34dd01d784e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-10(-1-2x)^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674231} {:answer/id #uuid "506242d7-6946-5793-af48-24427370b9ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-15(-1-2x)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674234} {:answer/id #uuid "cf3a5ea2-bbee-5c81-a219-c37346ebec71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-18(-1-2x)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674247}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674228} :answer-field/id #uuid "697835dc-03ad-5fb5-88bf-35beb7f43aa6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674237}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "41c093aa-391c-5ebf-acae-bdc80fe54491" :question/problem "Find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}$ when $f(x)=(-1-2x)^{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf=g^{3},\\,g=-1-2x\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=3g^{2},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=-2.\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} &=3\\cdot (-2)\\cdot (-1-2x)^{2} \\\\  &=-6(-1-2x)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674233 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38f7b679-b110-593d-9a4d-48c344350489" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6(-9+3x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674230}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674230} :answer-field/id #uuid "b127e32c-07a6-53ec-8d86-716356179dde" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674244}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4488b435-75c4-5bf8-836f-8c025405b71b" :question/problem "Find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}$ when $f(x)=(-9+3x)^{2}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf=g^{2},\\,g=-9+3x\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=2g,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=3.\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} &=2g\\cdot (3) \\\\  &=6(-9+3x).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674235 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "358cdd35-f54f-5f0a-96f8-8aa8b44b8ceb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-21(8-5x)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674229} {:answer/id #uuid "685dc9ff-3893-53af-a4fe-684701e82263" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-8(8-5x)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674236} {:answer/id #uuid "771e8765-6d6b-5ea7-b38e-82d4e23649c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6(8-5x)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674238} {:answer/id #uuid "a07bb43c-0d8b-56c9-bf60-bcb8516d2494" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-15(8-5x)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674242} {:answer/id #uuid "b5258c1e-66c7-5a68-9de6-0e14c158d25d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-20(8-5x)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674245}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674245} :answer-field/id #uuid "7917f945-dbcb-5a17-9d25-fe021a3c403f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674239}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5c07f75d-1f18-51f4-b433-e46bd0df0550" :question/problem "Find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}$ when $f(x)=(8-5x)^{4}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf=g^{4},\\,g=8-5x\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=4g^{3},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=-5.\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} &=4\\cdot (-5)\\cdot (8-5x)^{3} \\\\  &=-20(8-5x)^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674243 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "832f82b0-8996-58d2-aa20-2768c526e9b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12(5+3x)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674240}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674240} :answer-field/id #uuid "de68a7e9-8973-5b5b-b7b3-263757a2e394" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674249}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a25c900d-1561-5094-9272-47bf64ff1c06" :question/problem "Find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}$ when $f(x)=(5+3x)^{4}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf=g^{4},\\,g=5+3x\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=4g^{3},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=3.\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} &=4g^{3}\\cdot (3) \\\\  &=12(5+3x)^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674246 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1afff144-faa8-5d98-8b52-2e0fcc9a7f3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "30(-7+6x)^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674226} {:answer/id #uuid "1c35b387-63bd-565d-b5dc-feba286107ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "25(-7+6x)^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674227} {:answer/id #uuid "8ff15c7e-b33c-59b4-b72a-86eca43164f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "15(-7+6x)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674241} {:answer/id #uuid "d3e08094-b4f8-524a-b559-837c1a01dfd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "10(-7+6x)^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674248} {:answer/id #uuid "f771748e-0724-5882-9ec8-fdf9ce712c4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "18(-7+6x)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674251}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674226} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb94c143-3dce-569c-b7cf-c17c32239041" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674250}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c83476a7-334e-550f-a570-977c18f19b5f" :question/problem "Find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}$ when $f(x)=(-7+6x)^{5}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf=g^{5},\\,g=-7+6x\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=5g^{4},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=6.\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} &=5\\cdot 6\\cdot (-7+6x)^{4} \\\\  &=30(-7+6x)^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674306 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "255f9156-287e-5cc9-b8ed-eb31b15e83ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674307}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674307} :answer-field/id #uuid "b024a65a-2e57-571c-a34d-025276659956" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674316}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0a831727-2211-5532-89c4-e5a4ccb9ae4a" :question/problem "The slope of the tangent to the curve $y=\\sqrt{-7x+16}$ at the point where $x=0$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the slope at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nWe use the chain rule in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=-7x+16.$ Then $y=\\sqrt{u}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-7.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot -7 \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{-7x+16}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $x=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=0} & ={(-\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{-7x+16}})|}_{x=0} \\\\  & =\\frac{-7}{2\\sqrt{-7(0)+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-7}{2\\sqrt{16}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674308 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "767fa440-8fc1-5358-9025-7c8125e6aaa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674312}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674312} :answer-field/id #uuid "099a5827-9c3f-5cf3-bff5-003f736749ad" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674305}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2cf444c8-3239-54ca-9516-8df227c41a5f" :question/problem "The slope of the tangent to the curve $y=\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}+6x}$ at the point where $x=3$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the slope at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nWe use the chain rule in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=2{x}^{2}+6x.$ Then $y=\\sqrt{u}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4x+6.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot (4x+6) \\\\  & =\\frac{2(2x+3)}{2\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}+6x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x+3}{\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}+6x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $x=3,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=3} & ={(\\frac{2x+3}{\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}+6x}})|}_{x=3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4(3)+6}{2\\sqrt{2(3{)}^{2}+6(3)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{2\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674309 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c11f32b-69c1-5fd0-bddb-c652f4dd99dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674313}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186674313} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3399efe-ec83-56d2-bfb3-9ba448fc95b4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186674319}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "309f479d-646b-5563-8225-cb5faadfd4a1" :question/problem "The slope of the tangent to the curve $y=\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-7x}$ at the point where $x=4$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the slope at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nWe use the chain rule in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=4{x}^{2}-7x.$ Then $y=\\sqrt{u}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=8x-7.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot (8x-7) \\\\  & =\\frac{8x-7}{2\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-7x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8x-7}{2\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-7x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $x=4,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=4} & ={(\\frac{8x-7}{2\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-7x}})|}_{x=4} \\\\  & =\\frac{8(4)-7}{2\\sqrt{4(4{)}^{2}-7(4)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{2\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
